<article class="env-corollary" id="04P4">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04P4">Corollary <span data-tag="04P4">9.6.6.14</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category containing a pushout diagram </p>
<div class="equation" id="04P5">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="04P5" href="/tag/04P5">9.34</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:pushout-of-left-orthogonal} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ A \ar [r] \ar [d]^{f} &amp;  A' \ar [d]^{f'} \\ B \ar [r] &amp;  B'. } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p> If a morphism $g: X \rightarrow Y$ of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is right orthogonal to $f$, then it is also right orthogonal to $f'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      The diagram (<a data-tag="04P5" href="/tag/04P5">9.34</a>) determines a levelwise pushout square 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{id}_{A} \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{id}_{A'} \ar [d] \\ f \ar [r] &amp;  f' } \]
</div>
<p>
       in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{Fun}( \Delta ^1, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$. Since $g$ is right orthogonal to $f$, $\operatorname{id}_{A}$, and $\operatorname{id}_{A'}$ (Remark <a data-tag="06WA" href="/tag/06WA">9.6.6.9</a>), it is also right orthogonal to $f'$ (Proposition <a data-tag="06WC" href="/tag/06WC">9.6.6.12</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></article>
